        "market_text": "<p>Chicago's signature stock — vintage condos, greystones and two-flats — photographs with beautiful bones and empty, echoing rooms. Home staging warms the vintage details buyers love while proving the rooms hold modern furniture, the doubt that stalls showings on older stock.</p><p>Chicago is also fiercely seasonal: listings that launch in spring market weeks compete with everything else that waited for March. A staged listing stands out in the flood — and in the winter months, staged photos keep a listing feeling warm when the light outside is grey.</p><p>That seasonality is the real argument for staging virtually here. Physical staging in January means scheduling a truck and a crew through Chicago weather; the furniture also has to stay, and pay rent, for however long the listing sits in a slow month. Staging the photos instead removes both problems — the cost is fixed at {price:virtual-staging} a photo whether the listing moves in a week or sits until spring.</p>",
